{"id":"chatcmpl-44df5fe7-5b9b-4c88-ab43-e2ac2c797b90","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248458,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a medical image question requires inferring laterality from a lateral view, the successful strategy was to query multiple independent visual-question-answering tools with anatomically framed questions (anterior vs posterior, relation to heart/spine) and then map the lateral findings to frontal laterality via known anatomy. Cross-checking two tools' localizations before committing to an answer increased confidence. The key abstraction is decomposing a laterality question into an anatomical-localization sub-question, then applying domain knowledge to translate view-specific findings into the requested answer format.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Decompose a view-dependent question into an anatomical-localization sub-question (e.g., anterior vs posterior, relation to landmarks) before answering the original question.\",\n    \"Query multiple independent expert tools with the same anatomically framed question and require convergent localization before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Translate findings across imaging conventions using domain knowledge (e.g., lateral anterior field maps to a specific lobe/side on frontal view) rather than answering directly from the raw view.\",\n    \"Frame tool prompts to explicitly request the discriminating feature (which side/region) and the reasoning link to the target answer format.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Convert laterality/side questions into localization questions (anterior/posterior, landmark relations), then map to the requested side using anatomy; cross-check with a second tool.\",\n    \"Multi-tool consensus reasoning\": \"Ask each tool the same discriminating sub-question; only answer when localizations agree, and state the anatomical mapping as the justification.\",\n    \"Ambiguous-view inference\": \"When the image view doesn't directly show the answer, identify the intermediate anatomical fact that bridges the view to the answer, and query tools for that intermediate fact.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm both tools localize the finding to the same anatomical region before selecting an answer.\",\n    \"Verify the anatomical mapping rule (lateral region -> frontal side/lobe) is correctly applied to the requested answer format.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":467,"total_tokens":899,"completion_tokens":432,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":467},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":432}}}